 Reads boards/<name>/board.json and the CSV file it names ("data", relative to the board's folder) and writes
 boards/<name>/index.html. Rows are grouped into sections by the "section" field and ordered by the earliest date
 in each section; sections whose date has passed go under one fold at the bottom.
+
+Optional board.json keys (the events board uses none of them):
+- section with no "date": sections are ordered by name, with the empty one ("empty", e.g. "Nobody yet") first, and
+  rows inside a section are ordered by the first column marked "date".
+- a column with "date": true shows the date readably and, on rows not done, marks it overdue or due this week;
+  "format" wraps a value, e.g. "waiting on {}".
+- "done_label": rows whose status is done leave their sections and go under one fold with that label.
+- "rota": {"title", "date", "who", "empty"}: a list of weeks (the "date" field holds each week's Monday) shown at the
+  top, from this week on.
+Status values and section names are matched ignoring case, because the exports come from hand-typed spreadsheets.
 """
